        "declaredBy": "maintainer",
        "contact": null,
        "notes": "The REST API (wc/v3) sets no rate limit of its own: the shop is the merchant's own WordPress, and its host (a firewall, a security plugin, the hosting company) may limit it - a site adds that as its own tightening. WooCommerce's Store API rate limiting is opt-in and applies to the Store API only, which this provider does not call. The shop's data is the merchant's: redistribution depends on them."
